This feature adds a new method tag/template called `temporal-set`.

A Temporal Set is an Array-like data structure that only contains unique items, i.e., a "set," and has it's contents change over an indefinite length of time, i.e. "temporal."

This supports generated JavaScript APIs like this:

```javascript
const process = Module.find("Firebolt Tool",
  result => {
    console.log('this item shows up')
  },
  result => {
    console.log('this item goes away')
  }
)

setTimeout( () => { process.stop() }, 10000)

```

